366
00:20:42,021 --> 00:20:48,120
including D-Day at Normandy. The Germans had lined the shoreline

367
00:20:48,121 --> 00:20:52,160
with spikes that could tear up their bottoms.

368
00:20:52,161 --> 00:20:55,460
In addition, the heavily armed Germans defending the shore could

369
00:20:55,461 --> 00:20:59,260
have easily pulverized the slow-moving LVTs long before they

370
00:20:59,261 --> 00:21:04,080
reached the beaches. To help compensate for the LVTs'

371
00:21:04,081 --> 00:21:07,980
lack of speed, designers improved later models by adding more

372
00:21:07,981 --> 00:21:10,720
armor to their original quarter-inch thick plating.

373
00:21:15,720 --> 00:21:17,620
Today's expeditionary fighting vehicle

374
00:21:17,720 --> 00:21:20,620
is armored with a composite mesh material that

375
00:21:20,720 --> 00:21:25,040
is able to withstand 14.5 millimeter armor-piercing rounds

376
00:21:25,140 --> 00:21:31,780
fired from 300 meters. When it comes ashore,

377
00:21:31,880 --> 00:21:35,280
that tough stand comes in handy as the vehicle morphs from sea

378
00:21:35,281 --> 00:21:40,280
And even though it can't dance on the beach,

379
00:21:40,380 --> 00:21:43,780
it wears what's referred to as a hula skirt.

380
00:21:43,880 --> 00:21:46,520
What it's actually here for is to help dissipate heat

