00:37:39,641 --> 00:37:42,460
to the mother of all military movers.

668
00:37:42,461 --> 00:37:46,340
It's a giant vessel called the LMSR.

669
00:37:46,341 --> 00:37:50,520
That's short for Large, Medium Speed, Roll On, Roll Off,

670
00:37:50,521 --> 00:37:51,520
Ship.

671
00:37:51,521 --> 00:37:53,140
It's also known as a Roro.

672
00:37:55,080 --> 00:37:59,680
The Navy owns 19 LMSRs, and each is operated by a private

673
00:37:59,681 --> 00:38:03,120
company under contract to the Navy's Military Sealift

674
00:38:03,121 --> 00:38:03,821
Command.

675
00:38:06,620 --> 00:38:10,620
During the first six years after 9-11, LMSR ships transported

676
00:38:10,621 --> 00:38:14,940
more than 47 million square feet of cargo in support of US

677
00:38:14,941 --> 00:38:18,540
troops fighting the war on terrorism.

678
00:38:18,541 --> 00:38:21,740
That's equal to a trainload of ship containers stretching from

679
00:38:21,741 --> 00:38:25,240
stretching from Baltimore to Miami.

680
00:38:25,340 --> 00:38:30,280
Roro is basically a floating parking garage.

